# The R36S's sound output (package/jackswitch): "Playback Mux" held at HP,
# not moved by the headphone jack. Its device tree's jack line
# (rk3326-gameconsole-r3xs.dtsi, hp-det-gpios on gpio2 PC6, active high;
# the stock tree has it active low) read "plugged" whatever was in the jack
# on board R36S-V12 (Sylver, 2026-11-26), and neither ROCKNIX (no headphone
# device in its R36S quirks, 20260901) nor ArkOS or dArkOSRE reads it. HP
# is what ROCKNIX plays the R36S's speaker on (DEVICE_PLAYBACK_PATH_SPK="HP",
# packages/hardware/quirks/devices/Game Console R36S/001-device_config at
# its tag 20260901), and the headphones too, so both outputs play.
# zy_audio=SPK in r36s-boot.txt tries the class D speaker path instead.
OUTPUT=HP
